# ── orphan PERSISTENT journal sidecar locks (T-11062) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kernel filesystems hold no journal by construction, so they are the ONE thing excluded from the
# keep-set universe. Everything else in this mount namespace is walked — `/`, tmpfs, vfat, squashfs,
# and every container overlay — because a lock in THIS `/tmp` can only be minted by a process whose
# `/tmp` IS this one, i.e. one that resolves journal paths in THIS namespace.
#
# THE MEMBERSHIP TEST IS "CANNOT HOLD A USER-CREATED REGULAR FILE", NOT "feels like plumbing"
# (audit-post absorption). The first cut of this set also carried `ramfs`, `devtmpfs` and
# `fuse.gvfsd-fuse` — all of which DO hold ordinary files, so a live `events.jsonl` on one would have
# been missing from the keep-set while its same-uid sidecar in the temp root passed the orphan
# predicate. That is the one failure this whole category must not have. They are scanned now, like
# tmpfs and every overlay. The set is also a DENYLIST on purpose: an fstype nobody listed is WALKED,
# so an unfamiliar filesystem costs a scan rather than a wrongly reaped lock.
_PSEUDO_FSTYPES = frozenset((
    "proc", "sysfs", "devpts", "cgroup", "cgroup2", "securityfs", "pstore", "bpf",
    "tracefs", "debugfs", "hugetlbfs", "mqueue", "autofs", "binfmt_misc", "nsfs", "fusectl",
    "configfs", "efivarfs", "rpc_pipefs", "selinuxfs",
))


