# ── T-11511 (SPEC-0181) — the `bin/**` arm narrowed to an EXPLICIT, FAIL-CLOSED ALLOWLIST ────────
# `bin/**` is 37 modules and ~126k lines treated as ONE atom, while the runner and the selection
# ladder live in exactly two of them. MEASURED on this tree: of the 96 recorded refusals that carry
# `selection_full_suite_globs`, 85.4% matched `bin/**` ALONE; and of 235 first-parent commits since
# 2026-08-11 that touch `bin/`, 76 (32.3%) touch ONLY paths named below — every one of them forcing a
# full suite for a change that cannot alter how the runner runs tests. `bin/yitc-v2` alone is 69 of
# those touches and is a TWENTY-TWO LINE import-and-dispatch shim whose emptiness is already asserted
# by tests/test_t11319_thin_shim.py.
#
# THE DISCRIMINATOR IS POSITIVE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE SAFETY
# (lessons/carving-an-exception-into-a-fail-closed-gate). This enumerates what is FREED, by EXACT
# repo-relative path — never a prefix, never a filename shape, never "is not one of the known
# implementation modules". A path under `bin/` that nobody put here — a module added next month, a
# rename, a directory, a config file — matches nothing and keeps forcing the full suite. An
# allowlist that enumerated the EXCLUDED set instead would free a new module BY DEFAULT, which is the
# one direction that fails silently: tests would be omitted that should have run, and nothing would
# say so until something shipped broken.
#
# THE MEMBERSHIP TEST, stated so a future editor can apply it rather than guess: a path belongs here
# iff it neither RUNS the land's test suite nor PARTICIPATES in the selection decision — the two
# things rung R1 exists to protect. KEPT OUT, each for its own reason:
#   bin/lib/verify_runner.py — IS THE RUNNER (T-11519 moved it out of worktree.py; T-11520 proved the
#                           extraction complete in both directions). This is the ONE entry that must
#                           never appear in the list below, and T-11521 pins that in
#                           tests/test_verify_implementation_rule_narrowed.py rather than in a second
#                           production constant: the rule NAMES the runner, so its refusal stops
#                           resting on the fail-closed default that nobody had written down.
#   bin/lib/worktree.py   — the RESIDUE. It no longer defines `_run_verify_tests`, but it still holds
#                           the ladder's CALLERS (`_land_integrate`, `cmd_land`, `_run_pinned_verify`),
#                           the two freeing classifiers, and their module-level constants — which is
#                           why freeing it per FILE would free edits to the freeing rule itself. (It
#                           has its own, finer T-11463 fence above; that one PROVES non-participation
#                           per changed def rather than asserting it per file.)
#   bin/lib/rebaseline_currency.py — REFUSED ON LIMB A, and this is the membership test applied, not
#                           a leftover. T-11523 moved `_run_pinned_verify` here: it RUNS the land's
#                           pinned last-green suite (its line 776 calls the injected
#                           `_run_verify_tests(..., land_verify=True)` — "the pinned re-run is PART OF
#                           the land", T-11456). It also DEFINES `_pinned_cache_get`, whose True SKIPS
#                           that leg (consumed at `_land_integrate`, the `_pin_key` cache-HIT branch).
#                           So it both RUNS and GATES a verify leg. The keep-out property TRAVELLED
#                           WITH THE DEF: it is the same reason this comment already records for
#                           worktree.py ("still holds the ladder's CALLERS (… `_run_pinned_verify`)").
#                           Freeing it would narrow the candidate suite for exactly the diff able to
#                           neuter the driver that runs the pinned leg; today R1 forces the full suite
#                           there and catches it.
#   bin/lib/batch_landing.py — REFUSED ON BOTH LIMBS, and it is the only module in the population that
#                           fails limb B. LIMB B: it CONSUMES a selection root — `_shadow_select`,
#                           invoked by `_land_prequeue_known_broken_refusal` — and is injected
#                           `_is_verify_implementation_touch` UNDER THE ALIAS `_verify_touch` into
#                           `_land_cost_class` / `_land_batch_members`. That alias is why the test is
#                           read alias-aware: a by-NAME check of this file misses the real case.
#                           LIMB A: it DEFINES `_land_batch_verify_path_touch`, whose call-result the
#                           host binds to `_verify_path_touch`, and THAT variable gates whether the
#                           batch pays the pinned leg at all (`_land_integrate`); its own docstring
#                           names the stake — "under-firing is the circular-trust hole SPEC-0077
#                           exists to close". `_land_failure_attribution_probe` and
#                           `_land_red_isolation_probe` are additionally injected the runner and
#                           re-run tests during the land.
#
# THE TWO ENTRIES ABOVE ARE THE DELIVERABLE OF T-11654, NOT AN ASIDE — read them before filing "the
# extracted modules are missing from the allowlist" again. The T-11519..T-11525 split cut five modules
# out of worktree.py, and the natural reading is that all of them are periphery. They are not: applying
# THIS FILE'S OWN membership test to the three that were still absent admits exactly ONE. The derivation
# is mechanical and re-runnable, and it is pinned in `tests/test_t11511_bin_periphery_allowlist.py`
# (§AC1) rather than left as prose here, so it re-derives on every land instead of aging into a claim:
#   LIMB A — RUNS **or GATES** a verify leg of the land itself. Against the four names that do so
#     (`_run_verify_tests`, `_run_pinned_verify`, `_verify_path_touch`, `_pinned_cache_get`), a module
#     refuses if it DEFINES one of them, or defines a def whose call-result THIS FILE binds INTO one of
#     them (read off this module's own AST — that cross-module binding is limb A's alias-awareness, and
#     it is what catches batch_landing), or calls `_run_verify_tests(..., land_verify=True)`. Merely
#     BEING INJECTED the runner does NOT refuse — the `bin/lib/task.py` precedent above.
#   LIMB B — PARTICIPATES in the selection decision: the module references any `_SELECTION_DECISION_ROOTS`
#     name anywhere in its AST (call, bare reference, default, keyword argument or parameter name), the
#     same citation-by-name-IS-a-call-edge reading `_selection_participating_defs` documents.
#   It DISCRIMINATES, which is why its "no" means something: it re-derives every current member of the
#   list below as ADMIT with ZERO false refusals, while refusing verify_runner.py, worktree.py, cli.py
#   and the two entries above.
# THE ONE ENTRY T-11654 ADDED: `bin/lib/evidence_custody.py` — the journal-custody fold+restore the
# land runs THROUGH (`_fold_main_journal_into_branch` and the `_custody_*` reporters, extracted by
# T-11525). It is CLEAN ON BOTH LIMBS and each half was derived, not asserted: it defines none of the
# four verify-leg roots, defines nothing this file binds into one, never calls the runner at all, and
# references no `_SELECTION_DECISION_ROOTS` name under any alias. BEING ON THE LAND PATH IS NOT THE
# TEST and does not disqualify it — `bin/lib/events.py`, `bin/lib/journal.py`, `bin/lib/state.py` and
# `bin/lib/graph.py` are all on it and all freed; what the test asks is whether the module can change
# what the selector OMITS, and this one cannot. Honest second-order note, recorded rather than left for
# a reader to raise: its fold rewrites `events.jsonl`, which `_selection_recorded_misses` reads — but
# that exposure is SHARED with the already-audited `events.py` / `journal.py` members, so it is not a
# discriminator between them, and it is not the membership test this list is governed by.
#
# THE ONE ENTRY T-11522 ADDED, and it is the membership test above applied rather than an exception
# to it: `bin/lib/worktree_lifecycle.py` — the worktree-LIFECYCLE verbs (`worktree new` / `adopt` /
# `park` / `sweep` / `sync` / `recover-land`) and their exclusive mechanism, extracted from
# worktree.py. It NEITHER runs the land's test suite NOR participates in the selection decision, and
# both halves were proven mechanically against the PRE-move tree rather than asserted: none of the 42
# moved defs is in `_selection_participating_defs(worktree.py)` (29 defs, intersection empty), the
# module defines none of `_SELECTION_DECISION_ROOTS`, and it references no runner or selection symbol
# at all. WITHOUT this entry the extraction would REGRESS what it was cut to improve: a
# lifecycle-only change used to land in worktree.py, where the finer T-11463 fence could PROVE it
# non-participating and free it; moved to a `bin/` path in neither carrier it would match nothing and
# force the full suite every time. Note the coverage-map family and the floor-exclusion are DERIVED
# from this constant below — one edit, no second list to keep in step.
#   bin/lib/verify_wiring.py — hosts `_VERIFY_IMPLEMENTATION_GLOBS` itself and the verify wiring (T-12438 moved
#                           both out of bin/lib/cli.py, which is why cli.py is now FREED — see below).
#   bin/lib/init.py       — writes a consumer's verify-contract scaffolds.
#   everything non-`.py` under bin/ (audit-config.yaml, effort-routing-config.yaml,
#   pricing-config.yaml, git-maintenance.sh, verify-backup.sh, security-audit, v2-security-gate)
#   — and, by construction, anything not listed.
# THE ONE ENTRY A READER WILL QUESTION is `bin/lib/task.py`: `cmd_task_test` CALLS the injected
# `_run_verify_tests` for the `task test --run` verb. It is freed because calling the runner is not
# BEING the runner — it neither defines it nor feeds the land's selection decision, and `task test
# --run` is a caller selection never governs (`select` defaults False). Named here rather than left
# for a reader to rediscover.
#
# THE FOUR ENTRIES T-12155 ADDED, and the FIVE it deliberately KEPT OUT. Same membership test as
# above, re-run over every currently-unlisted `bin/*.py`; it returned 9 mechanical ADMITs, and each was
# then READ BY HAND, because the derivation is a FLOOR and not an oracle. Both halves are recorded,
# because a positive allowlist is only safe while every NEAR-MISS is on the record too — a reader who
# sees four names and no rejects cannot tell a judged list from an unjudged one.
#   ADMITTED AND FREED (clean on both limbs; each re-derives ADMIT on every land via §AC1 (i)):
#   bin/lib/release.py    — the RELEASE-SIGNATURE verify (`release` publishes the identity-agnostic
#                           view and checks its own signature). That word "verify" is the whole reason
#                           this entry is spelled out: it is a DIFFERENT verify from the land's test
#                           legs. It defines none of the four verify-leg roots, defines nothing the host
#                           binds into one, never calls the runner, and references no
#                           `_SELECTION_DECISION_ROOTS` name.
#   bin/lib/venue.py      — provisions/records the rented box (SPEC-0203's venue record). ZERO
#                           selection or runner references: it decides WHERE a leg could run, never
#                           WHETHER one runs nor WHICH tests are selected. The module that actually
#                           RUNS the legs on that box is `remote_verify.py`, and it is KEPT OUT below —
#                           the pair is the discrimination this entry rests on, not an oversight.
#   bin/lib/profile.py    — the machine/effort profile reader. Clean on both limbs.
#   bin/lib/host_paths.py — the declared-surface path resolver (SPEC-0187). Clean on both limbs; it
#                           resolves paths, it decides nothing about verify.
#   ADMITTED MECHANICALLY BUT KEPT OUT — each with the reason, FAIL-CLOSED on doubt:
#   bin/lib/remote_verify.py — IT RUNS THE LAND'S SUITE. SPEC-0203 rules 3-4: its ROUTING ENTRY
#                           ships the tree to the venue, runs BOTH SPEC-0077 legs there, and validates
#                           the verdict envelope. The derivation admitted it because limb A named only
#                           the FOUR pre-SPEC-0203 verify-leg roots and was therefore BLIND to the
#                           remote executor — a DEFECT IN THE FENCE, not a judgement call, captured as
#                           a deviation and FIXED in the same diff: T-12155 adds THAT ROUTING ENTRY
#                           to limb A's root set in `tests/test_t11511_bin_periphery_allowlist.py`, so
#                           this module now derives REFUSED rather than resting on this prose. A strict
#                           TIGHTENING — the added root can only ever refuse MORE. (The entry is
#                           named by its exact symbol THERE and only by DESCRIPTION here, which is
#                           not coyness: T-12194's `test_nothing_in_bin_calls_the_ROUTING_ENTRY`
#                           greps every `bin/**/*.py` for the literal token, so spelling it in this
#                           comment would read as a CALL SITE it plainly is not. Captured as a
#                           deviation — a guard whose stated intent is "nothing CALLS it" but whose
#                           mechanism is a text grep — rather than worked around in silence.)
#   bin/lib/machine_settings.py — decides each verify tunable's CLASS and holds a gate-class
#                           (`YITC_ISOLATED_VERIFY`); a class flip there is a live path from this module
#                           to HOW verify runs. Kept out on the substance, not on the derivation.
#   bin/lib/init.py       — SPEC-0181 R1's own prose NAMES it as still firing (it writes a consumer's
#                           verify-contract scaffolds — see the list above), while the mechanical
#                           derivation admits it. That is an artifact contradiction (CHARTER §P7),
#                           captured as a deviation and resolved FAIL-CLOSED for this card: the spec's
#                           answer wins, the module stays out. Reconciling the two needs its own card;
#                           it is worth 17 sole refusals in the measured window.
#   bin/lib/read_site_retirement.py — rewrites the read-set ledger the SPEC-0077 pinned probes assert
#                           against, so an edit here can change what those probes conclude.
#   bin/lib/worktree_batch_recovery.py — CLEAN on both limbs, and kept out anyway: ZERO occurrences in
#                           the measured window. CHARTER §P1 filter 3 — no evidence pulls it in, and an
#                           allowlist entry that frees nothing is dead weight that reads as coverage
#                           (the §AC2 existence arm above exists for the same reason).
#
# WHAT THIS CUT IS WORTH, stated plainly rather than dressed up: 341 -> 325 sole-refuser groups
# (-4.7%) over 2026-08-27..09-12. The DOMINANT refusers — `bin/lib/cli.py` (125 sole refusals) and
# `bin/lib/worktree.py` (56) — are refused on BOTH limbs precisely because they hold the verify wiring
# and the selection ladder, so freeing either per file IS the self-approval hole this rung exists to
# close. The real lever was to MOVE that wiring out of cli.py — T-12438 did, recorded next.
#
# T-12438 — bin/lib/cli.py ADMITTED, and bin/lib/verify_wiring.py KEPT OUT in its place. The membership
# test above, re-run on cli.py AFTER the move, derives ADMIT on both limbs (§AC1 (i) re-derives it on
# every land). What it refused on BEFORE, measured at Analysis, and why each ground is gone:
#   limb A — cli.py DEFINED `_run_verify_tests` and `_run_pinned_verify` (verify-leg roots) and
#            `_is_verify_implementation_touch` (a name this module binds into a verify-leg gate). All
#            three definitions moved to bin/lib/verify_wiring.py; cli.py now only PASSES the runner on,
#            which the test does not read as running a leg (the recorded bin/lib/task.py precedent).
#   limb B — cli.py DEFINED the selection root `_is_verify_implementation_touch`, and the decision
