# SPEC-0152 rule 16 (T-10303 / X-0140) — the SOURCE-LAYER MARKER registry for the layer-PRESENCE prompt.
# Each entry: (layer id, marker paths that PROVE that source layer exists in the tree). Born with the ONE
# family a real incident pulled (<project> shipped a frontend untested by a backend-only land gate); it
# GROWS when a new layer is actually pulled, never pre-emptively (CHARTER §P1 F4).
#
# A bare ROOT `package.json` is deliberately NOT a marker: a Node BACKEND declares one too, so it cannot
# distinguish the layers, and a false "frontend detected" would break the zero-false-positive stance the
# sibling coverage WARN holds. A `frontend/package.json` is unambiguous.
_SOURCE_LAYER_MARKERS = (
    ("frontend", ("frontend/package.json",)),
)


def _undeclared_source_layers(worktree: Path, ver) -> list:
    """SPEC-0152 rule 16 (T-10303 / X-0140) — the layer-PRESENCE check. Return the sorted
    `[(layer, marker), ...]` of source layers PRESENT in `worktree` (a `_SOURCE_LAYER_MARKERS` marker file
    exists) but ANSWERED by no `verify.layers` entry — the SILENTLY-ABSENT layers. `[]` = every detected
    layer is answered.

    ANSWERED means the layer appears in `verify.layers` at all — DECLARED (a `command:`) or WAIVED (a
    `waiver: {reason}`). Either silences the prompt; which one is right is the project's call, and the
    per-layer stance check (`_hook_verify` at init, the loop below at land) already polices the entry's
    shape. A declared layer whose `covers:` globs name that tree (a glob under `<layer>/`) also answers it —
    that layer says it verifies the surface, so the surface is not absent from the gate.

    The grow-trigger a waiver's `reason:` should record is NORMATIVE-only, never machine-checked: rule 3
    fixes that the kernel checks the declared STANCE + structural SHAPE, never the VALUE, and rule 6 makes a
    per-layer waiver LOOSE (a bare non-empty reason). Parsing prose for a "grow-trigger" is a value
    judgement any string defeats (audit-pre finding, absorbed mode-b).

    A SECTION-level `verify.waiver` does NOT answer a DETECTED layer. A fresh consumer is BORN
    section-waived, so honoring it here would silence the prompt in exactly the born-waived-consumer-with-a-
    frontend case X-0140 filed. A detected layer is answered PER LAYER.

    Pure + fail-OPEN: a malformed / absent `ver` yields no false "everything undeclared" — an unreadable
    carrier is the other guard branches' problem, never this report-only prompt's."""
    layers = ver.get("layers") if isinstance(ver, dict) else None
    answered: set = set()
    for ly in (layers if isinstance(layers, list) else []):
        if not isinstance(ly, dict):
            continue
        name = str(ly.get("layer") or "").strip().lower()
        if name:
            answered.add(name)
        for g in (ly.get("covers") or []):
            if isinstance(g, str) and "/" in g:
                answered.add(g.strip().split("/", 1)[0].lower())
    out: list = []
    for layer, markers in _SOURCE_LAYER_MARKERS:
        if layer.lower() in answered:
            continue
        hit = next((m for m in markers if (worktree / m).is_file()), None)
        if hit is not None:
            out.append((layer, hit))
    return sorted(out)


