# ── worker-liveness watchdog: the claim path's die-with-the-WORKER binding (T-11102, SPEC-0180 §3) ──
# `_arm_worker_land_pdeathsig` above binds this land's life to its IMMEDIATE PARENT. Under the `setsid`
# detach an admitted held-turn claim permits, that parent (the launcher shell) has already exited — so
# the pdeathsig binding is inapplicable by construction, which is exactly why the sanctioned
# long-command recipe is inadmissible for `land` today (SPEC-0180 rule 3). The binding must therefore
# name the WORKER process, and be asked of a PROCESS, not of a session ref (a ref outlives the process
# that minted it, so a watchdog keyed on it would never fire and the whole binding would be decorative).
#
# So: for a land ADMITTED under a verified claim, poll the SERVER-RESOLVED worker pid; the first read
# that is not 'alive' terminates this land. The termination happens while the land is still in its
# pre-integration phase in every realistic case (the ff-only merge is the LAST step, minutes after
# arming), so `main` is untouched and the branch is recovered by the existing idempotent
# `worktree recover-land` (T-10139) — no new recovery path.
#
# TRI-STATE, FAIL-CLOSED: 'dead' AND 'unprovable' both terminate. The pid was PROVEN alive at
# admission, so a later unanswerable read is a refusal, never an admission — the same rule `_pid_alive`
# states for the admission read, held on the same axis afterwards.
#
# THE KILL IS JOURNALED, AND THE WRITER COMES BY INJECTION (SPEC-0180 rule 3, learned the hard way).
# In this module the journal writer is a keyword-only `_append_event` injected into each command, so a
# module-scope helper CANNOT resolve it by name: the trial's first candidate killed correctly (exit
# 137) and emitted ZERO rows for exactly that reason, its try/except swallowing every record. A kill
# that cannot be seen re-creates the silent-death class `blocked-on-land` (SPEC-0103 §3) and the fleet
# verdict (SPEC-0133) exist to remove — from the controller's side it reads as a hang, not as correct
# enforcement. Hence: the writer is INJECTED, and when the record cannot be written the kill still
# happens AND says so LOUDLY on stderr.
_LIVENESS_WATCHDOG_POLL_SECS = land_reservation._LIVENESS_WATCHDOG_POLL_SECS   # T-12709 (C5b): moved to bin/lib/land_reservation.py — re-export alias


