# ── dispatched-worker land-verify progress heartbeat (T-9601, SPEC-0103 / T-9600 intent) ──────────
# The structural belt to T-9600's "a dispatched worker MUST foreground `land`" doc rule. The verify
# phase runs minutes-SILENT; that silence is exactly the timeout-fear that drives a headless worker to
# background `land` and then yield (its process exits → land dies mid-flight; T-9592/T-9593). In a
# DISPATCHED-worker context (the EXPECTED_SESSION_REF marker set by `dispatch`) `_run_verify_tests`
# streams a periodic progress line to STDERR, so the foreground run stays VISIBLY alive (keeps the
# harness command from reading as hung) + the worker is reassured not to background it — foreground by
# construction. The DOMINANT land verify (`_land_integrate` step-4) calls this IN-PROCESS, and
# `land --task` re-execs with subprocess.run + inherited stdio (no capture) — so the heartbeat reaches
# the worker's `land` command stderr in REAL TIME (audit-pre finding-2). STDERR keeps the
# `LAND: OK/ABORT` stdout-token contract (T-0269) clean. Additive, NON-gating: the verify VERDICT /
# per-file timeout (SPEC-0071) / gate (SPEC-0077) are untouched, and a non-worker context emits
# NOTHING (byte-identical to the pre-T-9601 behaviour). No new spec (the safety invariant is unchanged
# — SPEC-0005 admission test); doc home = AGENTS §Writes-happen worker land bullet (audit-pre finding-1).
