# ── T-11279 (SPEC-0184 rule 9) — THE ADDRESSED-YIELD OFFER ────────────────────────────────────────
# The yield was an UNADDRESSED release window: the holder dropped the reservation and whoever polled
# first won it, so the starving branch the yield was FOR could miss its own handover. Measured
# 2026-08-18: 4 yields fired while two class-0 branches degraded at their park limit. The offer below
# makes the handover ADDRESSED — it NAMES the successor, every other peer abstains for that window,
# and the addressee consumes the marker as it takes the slot.
#
# SAME CARRIER AS THE T-11274 SUPERSESSION MARKER, deliberately (CHARTER §P1 F1 — extend the analog):
# an off-tree file under the verify-slot dir, never committed, auto-scoped to one repo. But it is ONE
# FIXED PATH, not a per-branch hash, and that difference is load-bearing: a reader must answer «is an
# offer live, and is it for me?» in ONE cheap read, whereas a per-branch scheme needs a directory scan
# on the poll path — the wrong cost class for a loop that reads the flock and the clock and nothing
# else BY DESIGN (see `_land_supersession_marked`).
_LAND_YIELD_OFFER_NAME = batch_landing._LAND_YIELD_OFFER_NAME  # T-11524 host re-export alias — moved WITH its readers


