            # call, the same fail-closed guard) and reused here — one computation, one meaning.
            if _verify_path_touch and not bad and _pinned_policy_off:
                # T-11281 (SPEC-0186 rules 1+7): this project has DECLARED the leg off, so the gate that
                # would have applied does not run — and the land says so in its OWN word rather than
                # borrowing `candidate`. Not cosmetic: conflating "did not run" with "ran and passed" is
                # what made 15 of 30 decisive cases misread in the investigation that produced this
                # switch, so a policy-skip that recorded plain `candidate` would poison every future
                # measurement of this layer at source. Decided HERE and not at the step-4a preflight
                # (where the policy is resolved) because the batch union above can re-arm
                # `_verify_path_touch` AFTER that point — one authority, evaluated where it is used.
                # A land with NO verify-path touch stays plain `candidate`: nothing was skipped by
                # policy there, and saying otherwise would be the same conflation in the other direction.
                verify_mode = "candidate_policy_off"
                print("land: pinned last-green verify SKIPPED — this project declares "
                      "`verify_policy.pinned_last_green: never` (SPEC-0186 rule 1); "
                      "verify_mode=candidate_policy_off")
            elif _verify_path_touch and not bad:
                # The pinned last-green gate APPLIES on this land (via a warm cache hit OR a fresh
                # re-run) — record the truthful signal up front so both branches carry it.
                verify_mode = "pinned+candidate"
                # T-12151 — CONSUME THE PINNED-FIRST MEMO when the pre-step above already resolved this
                # land's pinned verdict, instead of resolving it a SECOND time. Re-probing here would be
                # wrong in a way that is invisible in the verdict but poisons the record: the pre-step
                # caches its own clean green, so a re-probe would HIT and this land — which really did
                # run the ~full pinned suite moments ago — would report `pinned_cache_hit`, i.e. exactly
                # the "did not run" vs "ran and passed" conflation the neighbouring
                # `verify_mode=candidate_policy_off` branch exists to prevent (SPEC-0186 rule 7). The
                # memo carries what ACTUALLY happened, so both fields stay truthful.
                if _pinned_first is not None:
                    pinned_bad, pinned_cache_hit = _pinned_first
                else:
                    pinned_bad, pinned_cache_hit = _resolve_pinned()
