        # above: it sits AFTER the verify-fail `_die`, so the T-0678 AC3 textual guard keeps meaning
        # exactly what it says, and the loop head then does the rest with no new machinery — it
        # resets the candidate to `_batch_pre_sha` (so the released peers' commits leave this
        # branch), re-forms with `solo_head=True` (so the head re-forms ALONE and cannot re-admit the
        # peers it just released), re-merges the CURRENT `main` and RE-VERIFIES IN FULL. That full
        # re-verify is the correctness bound, not an optimisation: the red run covered a tree that
        # included the peers, so the head holds no verdict of its own until it runs alone.
        if _peers_released:
            attempt_outcome = "retry-peers-released"
            continue
